From 1c97752ff84b3898d8485a090c46aafe8ef58c0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:41:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 429/429] hir_typeck: builtin `AsyncFn*` impls for callables
 returning a Future

cargo 0.99.0 (cargo-c 0.10.25) src/cargo/core/resolver/dep_cache.rs:256
`self.poller.poll(RegistryQueryerAsync::query, ..)` with
util/local_poll_adapter.rs:39 `F: AsyncFn(&S::Target, &K) -> Result<V, E>`
and `async fn query(&self, key: &(..)) -> CargoResult<..>`:
"Failed to find an impl of AsyncFnOnce<(&RegistryQueryerAsync<'_, T>, ..)>
for fn{RegistryQueryerAsync::query} with Output = Result<..>".

Since 1.85 rustc implements AsyncFn, AsyncFnMut and AsyncFnOnce itself
for closures, fn items and fn pointers whose return type is a Future
(`CallOnceFuture`/`CallRefFuture<'a>` are that type, `Output` its
`Future::Output`); core 1.90 ops/async_function.rs only has the `&F` and
`&mut F` forwarders, and mrustc only registered the lang items.

The Fn* arms of find_trait_impls_types (typeck) and find_impl (static)
now answer the AsyncFn* traits too when the return type is a Future,
plus a static arm for the post-expansion `closure#N` struct through its
Fn* impl. A value known only through AsyncFn* bounds is called as
`async_call`/`async_call_mut`/`async_call_once`: typeck gives it the
future type (`<F as AsyncFnMut<A>>::CallRefFuture<'_>`, or
`CallOnceFuture`), the validate, annotate-usage, lifetime and
ufcs_everything passes follow that choice, and trans enumerate plus MIR
cleanup rewrite `<callable as AsyncFn*>::async_call*` into the Fn* call
(closures have those impls, fn items and pointers then become direct
calls as before).

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
